   "title": "Novo Holdings, GIC, Axight look to back AIG Hospitals; Founders aim to pare 10-12% stake at Rs 24,000 cr v",
   "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"
  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "Novo Holdings, GIC, and Axight are in advanced discussions to invest Rs 2,000 to 2,500 crore in AIG Hospitals, a multi-speciality chain based in Hyderabad. The transaction involves a fund-to-fund transfer by EQT and a stake sale by the hospital chain's two founders, chairman and managing director Duvvur Nageshwar Reddy and vice chair Penmetsa Venkata Subbaraju. The founders plan to pare a 10% to 12% stake in the company at a valuation ranging from Rs 22,000 crore to Rs 24,000 crore. Goldman Sachs and UBS are advising on the transaction. The founders will continue to run the company.",
